# Local development configuration.
#
# LEAVE THIS FILE ALONE AND COPY NOTHING, and the app runs in demo mode:
# an in-memory fictional world, no backend, nothing written down. That is
# the right default for development and for browser previews.
#
# Production does NOT read this file. Production builds take their values
# from the EAS "production" environment (see supabase/production/README.md),
# so no key ever lands in git.
#
# Copy to .env only when you deliberately want your machine talking to a
# real Supabase project — and remember that means real writes.

# Force a mode regardless of the values below.
#   1 → always demo, even if a URL and key are present
#   0 → never demo; the app then REQUIRES the two values below
# Unset → demo when the two values are missing, live when they are present.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=1

# Project Settings → API. The anon key is a public client key — it is safe
# in an app bundle, and it is still not something to paste into a chat or
# commit to a repository.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
